      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Suggestion for a follow-up CL (to keep this move CL pure):**\n\nBecause the framework now only guarantees that `input_buf_size` is at least the size of `SMALLEST_TYPE(..., ec_params_fp_mode)` (the v0 struct size), a v1 command could theoretically be sent with a size smaller than `sizeof(ec_params_fp_mode_v1)`. This would cause an out-of-bounds read when accessing `p_1-\u003emac`. \n\nConsider adding an explicit size check for `v1` to prevent this:\n\n```cpp\n\tif (args-\u003eversion \u003d\u003d 1) {\n\t\tif (args-\u003einput_buf_size \u003c sizeof(struct ec_params_fp_mode_v1)) {\n\t\t\treturn EC_HOST_CMD_INVALID_PARAM;\n\t\t}\n\t\tconst auto *p_1 \u003d static_cast\u003cconst ec_params_fp_mode_v1 *\u003e(args-\u003einput_buf);\n\t\tmac \u003d std::span{ p_1-\u003emac };\n\t}\n``` [🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8464411_d9d266cf-ba11-4bf4-a3fe-a944414d30fc.pb)",
